<PageLayout title="SmartScreen Help — TotalRecalls" description="Windows SmartScreen guidance." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }, { label: "SmartScreen" }]}>
  <h1>SmartScreen Help</h1>
  <p>Windows SmartScreen may show a warning when you first run TotalRecalls. This is expected for unsigned apps.</p>
  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Click <strong>"More info"</strong> in the SmartScreen dialog.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>"Run anyway"</strong>.</li>
    <li>TotalRecalls will launch normally.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Why This Happens</h2>
  <p>SmartScreen uses reputation-based detection. New or uncommon executables trigger the warning. Once enough users run the app, the warning disappears automatically.</p>
  <p>Reputation builds as more people run the app, so the prompt fades over time rather than on a fixed schedule. If it keeps appearing, email <a href="mailto:support@totalrecalls.app">support</a> and we will look into it.</p>
</PageLayout>
